{"timestamp": 1779395825.206079, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I found Diana's body in Electrical. My route this round was Navigation to Security, and then I headed into Electrical where I immediately spotted her. \n\nI didn't pass anyone on my way there, and Security was completely empty. Since I didn't see anyone fleeing to the right side of the ship, the killer either vented out of Electrical, or they walked out towards Medbay or Cafeteria right before I got there. \n\nWhere was everyone else? Let's figure out who was on the left side of the map or near Cafeteria."}}
{"timestamp": 1779395838.025512, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I can confirm some details here. My route was Security, then Electrical, Medbay, and finally Upper Engine. \n\nDiana was definitely alive in Electrical when I was there\u2014I saw her there from tick 4 up until tick 6 when I left. Eve was also in Electrical around tick 4, but then I saw Eve in Medbay at tick 7, and she followed me into Upper Engine by tick 10. Because Eve's timeline matches up with walking between those rooms with me, I think Eve is pretty clear.\n\nSince I left Diana alive in Electrical at tick 6, she had to have been killed after that. Charlie, you say you found her there and didn't see anyone. That means the killer either went in right after I left and slipped out towards Cafeteria, vented, or... Charlie, it could be you if you walked in right after me. \n\nBob and Frank, we really need to know where you two were during all of this to narrow it down. Let's hear from you both before we vote."}}
{"timestamp": 1779395854.110543, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Alice, to answer your question, I was on the far left side of the ship the entire round, but I didn't see anyone at all. \n\nMy route was Upper Engine, up to Oxygen, back down through Upper Engine, and then into Lower Engine where I've been doing my tasks. Because I moved down to Lower Engine pretty early, it makes perfect sense that I didn't cross paths with you and Eve when you eventually made it to Upper Engine around tick 10. \n\nIf we trust Alice's timeline, that clears Eve. I know I'm innocent, and I was nowhere near Electrical. That really just leaves two possibilities: either Charlie is doing a self-report right now, or the killer is Bob, who is the only person completely unaccounted for so far. \n\nIf the killer slipped out of Electrical towards Cafeteria or Storage like Charlie suggested, Bob might have seen them\u2014or Bob might *be* them. We really need to hear your exact route, Bob. I'm holding my vote until we hear from you and Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779395884.1153212, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Thanks Frank, happy to clear this up. My route was Weapons, then Cafeteria, then Medbay \u2014 which is where I still am right now, you can see me on the map. I started in Weapons doing the calibration task, then cut through Cafeteria down to Medbay to submit my scan.\n\nI never went into Electrical this round, so I can't speak to what happened there directly. But a few things stand out to me:\n\nFirst, Charlie \u2014 you said Security was completely empty when you passed through. That actually lines up with my timing, because I went through Cafeteria, not Security, so we wouldn't have crossed. But it also means nobody can vouch for *your* movement between Security and Electrical. A self-report is absolutely on the table here.\n\nSecond, Alice, your timeline is very detailed and very convenient. You're the *last* confirmed person to see Diana alive in Electrical at tick 6, and you conveniently exit right before she dies. I'm not accusing yet, but \"I left right before the murder happened\" is a classic line.\n\nThird, Frank \u2014 you say you were in Lower Engine the whole back half of the round. Nobody can confirm that either. So let's not pretend only Eve is cleared here.\n\nI think we're between Charlie and Alice. I'm leaning Charlie for the self-report, but I want to hear Eve before I lock in my vote."}}
{"timestamp": 1779395901.222038, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I have the final piece of the puzzle, and I caught Bob in a massive lie. Bob is the Duck.\n\nBob, you just claimed you went from Cafeteria to Medbay and NEVER went into Electrical this round. That is completely false. I was in Medbay, and at tick 8, I literally watched you enter Medbay directly FROM Electrical! \n\nAlice's timeline is 100% correct. She and I were in Electrical with Diana around tick 4, we moved to Medbay, and then headed towards Upper Engine. After Alice and I left Electrical, Bob was in there with Diana. He killed her, and then slipped out into Medbay at tick 8 right before Charlie found the body. \n\nHe is lying about his path to hide the fact that he was at the scene of the crime. Charlie's theory about the killer walking out towards Medbay was spot on. We are voting Bob right now."}}
